{"step_index":991,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:33:56Z","thinking":"**Verifying Lemma Correctness**\n\nThe Lean 4 code compiles without errors, indicating the lemma is well-formed. The provided lemma `finset_min_getD_le` establishes a lower bound for an element of a finite set with its minimum value. The proof strategy hinges on showing the minimum is less than or equal to an element of the set using `Finset.inf_le`. This inequality is then case-split, and rewritten to deduce the desired result. The use of `WithTop` seems important for handling potential empty set scenarios.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > scratch.lean\\nimport Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nlemma finset_min_getD_le {s : Finset ℕ} {b : ℕ} (hb : b ∈ s) :\\n    s.min.getD 0 ≤ b := by\\n  have h : s.min ≤ WithTop.some b := Finset.inf_le hb\\n  cases hm : s.min with\\n  | top =>\\n    rw [hm] at h\\n    simp at h\\n  | coe m =>\\n    rw [hm] at h\\n    exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp h\\n\\nlemma radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\\n  apply finset_min_getD_le\\n  apply Finset.mem_image.mpr\\n  exact ⟨v, Finset.mem_univ v, rfl⟩\\nEOF\\n/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh scratch.lean\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_2a2555cc\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Testing radius_le_eccentricity\"","toolSummary":"\"Test radius_le_eccentricity\""}}]}
